## 04a27ff51304

**Reproduced teaching ambiguity: three demonstrations can fail to identify the same-color requirement.** Current generator SHA-256: `d9e6c8d15eae0c2505749ea4eb92ca5b29036c416fc3c13a017e0eb9194d9101`; executed rule hash: `f3a3e1a37f60`.

For seed 0, default difficulty, and sample indices 0–3, the rival “paint every cell where nonzero occupancy forms both a horizontal run of length at least 3 and a vertical run of length at least 3, ignoring run colors” matches the authoritative Racket outputs on the first three pairs. It differs on the fourth pair at exactly cell `(6,1)`: the rival paints an 8 at a different-color crossing that the canonical same-color rule leaves 0. All four generated inputs pass `self_check`.

Fresh source-bound evidence is in:

- `checks/audit/04a27ff51304/generated.json` and `input.json` — seed/sample identities, source hash, and validator results;
- `checks/audit/04a27ff51304/racket.json` — canonical Racket outputs;
- `checks/audit/04a27ff51304/rival-output.json` and `shortcut-repro.json` — exact rival outputs, one-cell query difference, and `[true,true,true,false]` agreement vector;
- `checks/audit/04a27ff51304-combined/result.json` — isolated audit preset.

The isolated preset reports no selected task tests and fails the strict semantic gate because no executable semantic contract is declared. Recommended repair: guarantee that each self-contained lesson includes both a same-color positive crossing and a different-color decoy crossing, then declare and test the occupancy-only rival under every supported query rotation. No source was changed in this audit.
